 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply our\nDays of our youth will end forever; when\nI'm no more, but found alone afar\nIn the dark desert; I have left again\nThe warm and green resting-place for ever\nWhere once the old days were a delight.  Where\nMy heart is gathering round me never\nTo trod his own path where the deeper air\nHas not its crosstrees for my lingering feet,\nThen wander'd down in those quiet days,\nBy the little stream which by evening\nGoes silently thro' the winding shady",
